@startuml
title Small Baby-Safe Robot – System Architecture (V1)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

package "Power" {
  [Battery\n(2S Li-ion\n7.4–8.4 V)]
  [Motor Power Rail\n(~9 V max)]
  [Buck Converter\n5 V]
  [LDO / Buck\n3.3 V]
}

package "Compute" {
  [Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux]
  [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]
}

package "Communication" {
  [CAN Bus\n(or UART for V1)]
}

package "Motion Control" {
  [Motor Drivers\n(H-Bridge)]
  [Drive Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox]
  [Steering Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox]
  [Encoders\nx8\n(Drive + Steering)]
}

package "Programming & Debug" {
  [SWD Header]
  [BOOT0 Control]
  [RESET Control]
}

' Power connections
[Battery\n(2S Li-ion\n7.4–8.4 V)] --> [Motor Power Rail\n(~9 V max)]
[Battery\n(2S Li-ion\n7.4–8.4 V)] --> [Buck Converter\n5 V]
[Buck Converter\n5 V] --> [Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux]
[Buck Converter\n5 V] --> [LDO / Buck\n3.3 V]
[LDO / Buck\n3.3 V] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]

' Communication
[Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux] --> [CAN Bus\n(or UART for V1)]
[CAN Bus\n(or UART for V1)] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]

' Motion control
[STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control] --> [Motor Drivers\n(H-Bridge)]
[Motor Power Rail\n(~9 V max)] --> [Motor Drivers\n(H-Bridge)]

[Motor Drivers\n(H-Bridge)] --> [Drive Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox]
[Motor Drivers\n(H-Bridge)] --> [Steering Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox]

[Drive Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox] --> [Encoders\nx8\n(Drive + Steering)]
[Steering Motors\nx4\nDC + Gearbox] --> [Encoders\nx8\n(Drive + Steering)]
[Encoders\nx8\n(Drive + Steering)] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]

' Programming / OTA flashing
[Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux] --> [BOOT0 Control]
[Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux] --> [RESET Control]
[BOOT0 Control] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]
[RESET Control] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]

[SWD Header] --> [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]

note right of [STM32 MCU\nReal-time Control]
- Closed-loop motor control
- Encoder feedback
- Safety watchdog
- Stops motors if comms lost
end note

note right of [Raspberry Pi 4/5\nLinux]
- High-level logic
- Kinematics
- Networking / UI
- OTA firmware flashing
end note

@enduml
